+# TASK-260720-1qhxqa — developer handoff evidence
+
+## Outcome
+
+Ready for independent review. The immutable machine manifest is
+`Configuration/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`; its
+recomputed SHA-256 is
+`39b3428d6cf778fa6b682bb0853a177d6b85f03b8062309f0d198dcdfd49fae6`.
+The authoritative validation report records
+`productionCompositionPermitted=true` with no failing rows.
+
+## Exact accepted-resource bindings
+
+| Authority | Accepted outcome and SHA-256 | Reviewer verdict and SHA-256 | Acceptance | Supersession |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `TASK-260715-nphtib` | `TASK-260715-nphtib_results.md` — `63faf7a35b1c3554bbe5c23def6edddb9bc8454d40bfc1fb94071e1461f23ddd` | `TASK-260715-nphtib_final-delta-review-results.md` — `d9278fb1baec644d27c2fbd4a263758dee8f583b796f9c8ae7cc5e2e80985679` | accepted 2026-08-19, date precision | current |
+| `TASK-260715-2jatnd` | `TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md` — `f2dc587541386cdc5eb7e10328adda21b8bbba3af32d5c722e62616a2abca173` | `TASK-260715-2jatnd_review-verdict-rev2.md` — `73de6f96adadbd4b9469e26d760c3edbe6bd56120b97ab4f3d752812d3df8246` | accepted 2026-08-29, date precision | current |
+| `TASK-260715-1gjxer` | `TASK-260715-1gjxer_ssh-engine-selection-adr.md` — `f1d2369a694c7a6f6642cff4324b46a6727b7a6aef3d65a9cf13ee8821ea2282` | `TASK-260715-1gjxer_results.md` — `3583369777a0d897ef2a156ddddeea92cd15b5c0b3b290582015667a37044a31` | accepted 2026-08-18, date precision | current |
+| `TASK-260715-30zng6` | `TASK-260715-30zng6_runtime-contract.md` — `c13bbb54a455da89f3e66121c81532b298eab73fac30b6d14d2e2df43fff8851` | `TASK-260715-30zng6_review.md` — `7a64ad098efd8cff52e0c6d144763b29e4d4008aab8e0967ce805c6134b0b756` | accepted 2026-07-20, date precision | current |
+
+The board projection independently confirms all four authority tasks remain
+`done` and every named resource remains declared. The manifest separates each
+binding outcome from its reviewer verdict; no note, source default, producer
+handoff, rejected revision, or inferred value is treated as authority.
+
+## Normalized conditions and compatibility
+
+The machine manifest includes the exact generated graph and revisions;
+PacketFlowBridge and five-part HEV/lwIP pin set; MTU, requested/effective buffer,
+batching, HEV stack/TCP/UDP-copy/session, memory, notice, and no-fork conditions;
+the selected libssh2/OpenSSL adapter and pins; primary/fallback algorithms;
+window/buffer/rekey/lifecycle values; mandatory capabilities; license,
+maintenance, advisory, rebase, and revalidation obligations; rejected/deferred
+states; and eight stable compatibility rows against `m1-runtime-contract/1`.
+
+`TASK-260715-3ejhyy` receives this exact JSON as a precondition and must consume
+it as the sole M0 binding source. Its future production factory entry point must
+validate before constructing concrete SSH, PacketFlowBridge, or HEV dependencies
+and before `NetworkSettingsApplier.apply`.
+
+## Fail-closed and negative evidence
+
+The production CLI validator rejects:
+
+- changed upstream bytes, missing resources, malformed/unreadable manifest;
+- reopened tasks, undeclared resources, and explicit supersession;
+- unknown fields/schema, any set other than all three M0 inputs, and a stored
+  permit inconsistent with recomputation;
+- negative/missing/duplicate compatibility rows;
+- generated provider graph, HEV pin, libssh2 pin, or OpenSSL pin drift.
+
+The named narrowing test removes one of three M0 inputs and still requires exit
+1/permission false. The changed-resource test modifies accepted bytes without
+changing the old digest and requires exit 1, proving an upstream replacement
+cannot silently retain permission. Absence and malformed read have distinct
+stable failure rows.
+
+## Validation exits
+
+| Gate | Exit | Evidence |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| `make m0-bindings-check TASK_BOARD_RESOURCES=/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/m0-bindings-check-01.log`; permit true, zero failures |
+| `make m0-bindings-test` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/m0-bindings-test-01.log`; 11 tests passed |
+| Python compile + JSON parse + `git diff --check` | 0 | task-scoped syntax/lint logs |
+| `swift-format lint --strict --recursive ...` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/swift-format-lint-01.log` |
+| `make check-core-boundaries` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/core-boundaries-01.log` |
+| `make check-native-dependencies` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/native-dependencies-01.log` |
+| `swift build` | 0 | `.temp/TASK-260720-1qhxqa/swift-build-01.log`; existing `SecKeychainCopyDomainDefault` deprecation warning only |
+| `swift test --filter ProviderAdapterContractTests` | 0 | 14 tests passed |
+| `swift test --filter ReluxLibSSH2PackagingTests` | 0 | 3 tests passed |
+| `swift test --filter NativeDependencyPackagingTests` | 0 | 1 test passed |
+
+No M0 matrix was rerun. Existing physical/real-host evidence was consumed only
+through its accepted outcomes. No signing, installation, application/provider
+launch, VPN preference save, tunnel activation, route change, DNS change, or
+NetworkExtension operation was performed.
